---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Fewer Photos Works"
  description="Review your library month by month, keep or queue each item, then confirm deletions when you are ready."
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
    <h1>A large camera roll, broken into small decisions.</h1>

    <p class="introduction">
      Fewer Photos organises your library by month and presents one item
      at a time. There are no automatic deletions and no pressure to finish a
      review in one sitting.
    </p>
  </section>

  <figure class="workflow-preview">
    <img
      src="/hero-library.jpeg"
      alt="Fewer Photos showing a camera roll organised into monthly photo collections."
    />

    <figcaption>
      Choose a month and continue from exactly where you stopped.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <section class="steps" aria-label="Fewer Photos review process">
    <article>
      <span>01</span>
      <h2>Choose a month</h2>
      <p>
        Your photo library is arranged into manageable monthly collections.
        Start with yesterday, last summer or a forgotten year.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>02</span>
      <h2>Review one item</h2>
      <p>
        Swipe or use the clear controls to keep an item or place it into
        the Review Queue.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>03</span>
      <h2>Change your mind</h2>
      <p>
        Undo the most recent choice at any time. Favouriting is also available
        without leaving the review.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>04</span>
      <h2>Return when ready</h2>
      <p>
        Progress is saved automatically. Close the app halfway through a month
        and continue from the remaining items later.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>05</span>
      <h2>Check the queue</h2>
      <p>
        Every item marked for deletion remains visible in a separate queue.
        Restore individual items before confirming anything.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article>
      <span>06</span>
      <h2>Confirm with Apple Photos</h2>
      <p>
        Fewer Photos only requests deletion after you explicitly confirm the
        queue. Apple Photos then presents its own system confirmation.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="review-styles">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Choose your controls</p>
      <h2>Use the review style that feels natural.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="style-grid">
      <article>
        <div class="gesture vertical">
          <span class="keep">Keep ↓</span>
          <div class="photo-card">Photo</div>
          <span class="delete">Delete ↑</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Vertical Review</h3>
          <p>
            Swipe down to keep and up to queue for deletion. Designed for
            comfortable one-handed use.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article>
        <div class="gesture horizontal">
          <span class="delete">← Delete</span>
          <div class="photo-card">Photo</div>
          <span class="keep">Keep →</span>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h3>Classic Swipe</h3>
          <p>
            Swipe left to queue for deletion and right to keep. Familiar,
            direct and available from Settings.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="safety-panel">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Built around deliberate deletion</p>
      <h2>Queued first. Deleted only after confirmation.</h2>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p>
        Fewer Photos never silently removes an item. Your queue remains
        reviewable until you choose to continue, and Apple provides the final
        system-level deletion prompt.
      </p>

      <a href="/support">Read common questions</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    max-width: 54rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 10vw, 7rem);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--colour-accent-bright);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 13ch;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .introduction {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 2vw, 1.3rem);
  }

  .workflow-preview {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(4rem, 10vw, 7rem);
    padding: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    border-radius: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--colour-surface);
    box-shadow: 0 1.5rem 4rem rgba(44, 54, 42, 0.08);
  }

  .workflow-preview img {
    width: 100%;
    max-height: 48rem;
    display: block;
    object-fit: contain;
    border-radius: 1rem;
  }

  .workflow-preview figcaption {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--colour-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .steps article {
    min-height: 18rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    border-radius: 1.3rem;
    background: color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--colour-surface) 88%,
      transparent
    );
  }

  .steps article > span {
    width: 2.25rem;
    height: 2.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--colour-coral-soft);
    color: var(--colour-coral);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .steps h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.55rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
  }

  .steps p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .review-styles {
    padding-block: clamp(6rem, 13vw, 10rem);
  }

  .section-heading {
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }

  .section-heading h2 {
    max-width: 15ch;
  }

  .style-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .style-grid article {
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    border-radius: 1.4rem;
    background: var(--colour-surface);
  }

  .gesture {
    min-height: 17rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    background: var(--colour-surface-raised);
    color: var(--colour-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .gesture.vertical {
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .photo-card {
    width: 8rem;
    height: 10rem;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border: 0.35rem solid var(--colour-surface);
    border-radius: 0.9rem;
    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 68% 28%,
        #f4d88f 0 8%,
        transparent 9%
      ),
      linear-gradient(145deg, #89a9c0, #d8937e);
    box-shadow: 0 0.8rem 2rem rgba(38, 45, 37, 0.15);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
  }

  .keep {
    color: var(--colour-accent-bright);
  }

  .delete {
    color: var(--colour-coral);
  }

  .style-grid h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }

  .style-grid p {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .safety-panel {
    padding: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.85fr) minmax(18rem, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--colour-border);
    border-radius: 1.5rem;
    background:
      radial-gradient(
        circle at 5% 5%,
        rgba(217, 130, 130, 0.16),
        transparent 18rem
      ),
      var(--colour-surface);
  }

  .safety-panel h2 {
    max-width: 13ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .safety-panel p {
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .safety-panel a {
    color: var(--colour-accent-bright);
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .safety-panel a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  @media (max-width: 46rem) {
    .steps,
    .style-grid,
    .safety-panel {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .steps article {
      min-height: auto;
    }

    .steps article > span {
      margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    }

    .gesture.horizontal {
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
